	(text "Format : 0 = NTSC / 1 = PAL\n\nNTSC = 262 lines\nPAL = 312 lines"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.246 14.986 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c07ff280-2fed-4f20-bbed-7c79e4a74f90")
	)
	(text_box "Module counts X pixels (clock ticks) and Y rows of the screen\n\nX is clocked off a regular 14.31818MHz (NTSC colour clock * 4) commonly used in 8-bit computers\n\nThe function of the module crosses over into the limits of screen resolution by defining the reset boundaries for the counters.\n\nAdditionally the vertical screen resolution is configured to be capable of switching between NTSC and PAL timing and resolution\n\nNTSC assumes 262 lines in interlace mode at 60Hz (equivalent to 525 lines at 30Hz for progressive)\nPAL assumes 312 lines in interlace mode at 50Hz (625 lines at 25Hz for progressive)\n\nHorizontal resolution remains the same for both formats at 916 clock cycles (fractionally under 64uS)\nChanging the clock frequency requires recalculating the resolutionto retain 64uS row timing\n\nThe number of clock cycles is 64/(1/clock)\nWhere clock is the frequency in MHz\n\nThe bit pattern of the clock cycles count (rounded down) is mapped into U10 to generate the horizontal reset\n\nProvided the row timing of 64uS is respected there is no need to change the row reset calculation"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 86.36 0)
		(size 66.04 67.31)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "94657954-9be9-4e9c-ab43-dd319ab37cb4")
	)
